From f34e54388d6586c0ddd606c2991dd15ab0b0ef85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samuel <samuelMadureira23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:18:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] allstars: apply ColinGamez/allstars-ps3 runtime patch +
 fix sys_lwcond_t layout

The allstars-ps3 patch adds 8 missing HLE handlers (cellSpursJq attrs,
_sys_spu_printf). On top of it, sys_lwcond_create/wait in ppu_sysprx.cpp
treated sys_lwcond_t as {be64 lwmutex; be32 id @+8}. The real layout (and
sys_lwcond_t_hle) is {be32 lwmutex; be32 lwcond_queue}. The be64 write left
the first word zero, so FIOS (which embeds the lwcond at cond+0x10 and treats
a zero first word as 'invalid cond') spun forever at boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
